# Dusk environment files: the local # ===========================================================================
# DATABASE PROTECTION (see AGENTS.md)
#
# `.env.testing` and `.env.dusk.local` point the suite at a DISPOSABLE database.
# They are ignored for the same reason `.env` is: they hold an APP_KEY and are
# per-machine. `.env.testing` is committed ONLY when it contains no real secrets.
# ===========================================================================
.env.testing
# Dusk environment files: the local .env.dusk.local holds a real APP_KEY and
# must never be committed; CI generates .env.dusk on the runner.
.env.dusk
.env.dusk.*
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
/.fleet
/.idea
/.nova
/.phpunit.cache
/.vscode
/.zed
/auth.json
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
# SQLite databases are per-environment state, never source. Committing one would
# let a local snapshot overwrite (or be shipped into) the production database.
#
# THIS INCLUDES THE TEST DATABASES. `testing.sqlite` and `dusk.sqlite` are
# disposable artifacts of a test run, never fixtures to be shared.
/database/*.sqlite
/database/*.sqlite-journal
/database/*.sqlite-wal
/database/*.sqlite-shm
/database/*.sqlite.pre-safety-backup
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL-ONLY MOCK / DEMO DATA.
#
# MockDataSeeder creates five institutions' worth of realistic sample data
# (members, deposits, meals, expenses, subsidies, vendors, menu votes, claims).
# It is deliberately NOT tracked by git: keeping the file out of the repository
# makes it IMPOSSIBLE to deploy the sample dataset to production, rather than
# merely discouraged. A `--demo` flag on the committed DatabaseSeeder would ship
# the fixture data (names, phone numbers, fake ledgers) with the source, and a
# single `php artisan db:seed` on a live system could then create it.
#
# Run it locally with:
#     php artisan db:seed --class=MockDataSeeder
# Remove it again with:
#     php artisan db:clear-dummy --force
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/database/seeders/MockDataSeeder.php
# Command Code: share the deliberate stack agents, but NOT machine-local config
# or the auto-learned taste preferences.
/.commandcode/settings.json
/.commandcode/taste/
# Command Code LSP/scratch artefacts.
/storage/framework/lsp-*.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
